70 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186279504 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280870 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "158dba50-6c99-530b-a3b4-71c1f3ef60c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278597 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186278688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186279401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186280191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186278688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186280923 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "30341de0-d7c9-531a-935d-0764a34a14a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281352 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186280870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281352 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161838" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281352 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281352 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281352 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "613ff480-77bb-508e-adea-361b7545c613" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186281352 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ {u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2u & 2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (2v)-(2u)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2v-2u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2v-2u & <0 \\\\ 2v & <2u \\\\ v & <u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv=u\n$$\n\ndefines a straight line, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/83/8382e54c1f91ff0e07910c1250c046413814748d9e7ef8968984b7223b43afcc.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369876 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186369879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186369875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369874 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c478e331-2d1a-585a-9599-198d7061ae49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186369875 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1